%N A400539 Number of lattice points of the tetrakis hexahedron whose vertices are (+-3n,0,0), (0,+-3n,0), (0,0,+-3n) and (+-2n,+-2n,+-2n).
%C A400539 The tetrakis hexahedron is the cube [-2n,2n]^3 with a square pyramid of height n on each face; it is the dual of the truncated octahedron (A371515). It is the set of points (x,y,z) with 2|x| + |y|, 2|x| + |z|, 2|y| + |x|, 2|y| + |z|, 2|z| + |x| and 2|z| + |y| all at most 6n.
%C A400539 For n >= 1, it has 96*n^3 - 24*n^2 + 10*n - 1 interior lattice points and 48*n^2 + 2 boundary lattice points.
%H A400539 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-6,4,-1).
%F A400539 a(n) = 96*n^3 + 24*n^2 + 10*n + 1.
%F A400539 G.f.: (1 + 127*x + 367*x^2 + 81*x^3)/(1 - x)^4.
%F A400539 E.g.f.: exp(x)*(1 + 130*x + 312*x^2 + 96*x^3).
%F A400539 a(n) = 4*a(n-1) - 6*a(n-2) + 4*a(n-3) - a(n-4) for n >= 4.
%e A400539 For n = 1 the tetrakis hexahedron has 131 lattice points, of which 81 are interior and 50 are on the boundary.
%o A400539 (PARI) a(n) = 96*n^3 + 24*n^2 + 10*n + 1
%o A400539 (Python) def a(n): return 96*n**3 + 24*n**2 + 10*n + 1
%Y A400539 Cf. A046142, A371515, A371532.
%K A400539 nonn,easy,new
